 ("docs/manuscript/draft/fig5_discussion.md", "93-97",
  "The native RNA–genetics interface contains 14,704 genes: 426 genetically\nsupported and 1,155 canonical disease-state calls, with 26 in both compared\nwith 33.46 expected under independent membership (odds ratio 0.757, nominal\nFisher P=0.200). Non-overlap is 93.90%, against 92.14% expected from these set\nsizes. This is an arithmetic comparison, not evidence that the biological\nprocesses are independent.",
  "Among the 3,769 genes of the native RNA–genetics interface evaluated by\nmulti-signal colocalization, 426 are genetically supported and 220 are\ncanonical disease-state calls, with 26 in both against 21.21 expected for genes\nof the same expression level (Mantel-Haenszel odds ratio 1.295, 95% CI 0.835 to\n2.007; exact stratified P=0.2755, one prespecified test). Expression was not\nfully controlled by the 10 bins, so no direction is read from this, and odds\nratios between about 0.46 and 1.77 could not be detected at 80% power. A\nfurther 935 disease-state calls had no multi-signal colocalization result and\nare not genetic negatives. This is an arithmetic comparison, not evidence that\nthe biological processes are independent."),
 ("docs/PAPER.md", "575-588",
  "- The named genetic and bulk disease-state sets are largely non-overlapping, at\n  approximately the rate independent sampling produces for two sets of their\n  sizes (26 shared against 33.4 expected in the raw symbol-grouped,\n  pre-adjudication universe of 14,720 jointly testable genes,\n  426 genetic and 1,155 disease-state; 93.9% non-overlap against 92.2%\n  expected; odds ratio 0.76, nominal p 0.20). These values use the adopted\n  774-unit bulk refit and COLOC release `susie_coloc_r2_20260924T053244Z`,\n  adopted on October 14. The primary stable-Ensembl interface contains 14,704\n  genes and the annotation-adjudicated Catalog contains 14,682; these universes\n  must not be interchanged.",
  "- Among the 3,769 genes evaluated by multi-signal COLOC, the 426 colocalized\n  and 220 canonical disease-state genes share 26, against 21.21 expected for\n  genes of the same expression level (10 AveExpr bins; Mantel-Haenszel OR\n  1.295, 95% CI 0.835 to 2.007; exact two-sided P 0.2755; H57, one\n  prespecified test). A matched negative control showed that the bins do not\n  fully remove expression confounding, so no direction may be stated. The data\n  cannot distinguish independence from an odds ratio anywhere between about\n  0.46 and 1.77 (80% power); \"at chance\" may be written only with the interval\n  and this limit. The earlier 26 against 33.4 (OR 0.76) counted 10,928 genes\n  without a multi-signal COLOC result, 935 of them canonical DEGs, as genetic\n  negatives and is withdrawn. These values use the adopted 774-unit bulk refit\n  and COLOC release `susie_coloc_r2_20260924T053244Z`, adopted on October 14.\n  The 14,704-gene stable-Ensembl interface, the 14,720 symbol-grouped rows and\n  the 14,682-gene adjudicated Catalog are distinct universes and must not be\n  interchanged."),
